      "content": "1. Nature of the Revolt"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Revolt of 1857 was driven by cumulative political, economic, social, religious, and military causes.",
        "The immediate cause triggered the beginning and spread of the uprising across key regions.",
        "Prominent leaders spearheaded the rebellion in different regions, though regional limitations contributed to its ultimate failure.",
        "The consequences led directly to major administrative restructuring via the Government of India Act 1858."
      ],
